      "message": "[warning] Line 79: 🟡 `Tables` is an array of raw pointers indexed by `Policy`, and `evaluate()` dereferences it unconditionally. If a new `Policy` value is added but its table is forgotten, the default-initialized pointer entry will be `nullptr`, causing a crash instead of a safe deny/unknown decision. Store tables by value (`std::array\u003cPolicyTable, PolicyCount\u003e`) or add a null-check/static_assert so policy extensions fail safely.",
